# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a function of a block reads the block's names and its own parameters), ch. 8 (the first clause the arguments match is built, transparent) and ruling TC (places are counted as built): `@Row 0` builds one label and gives $count + 1; `@Row 2` builds its own label and then the labelled one, which shows $count + $count and gives one more; the click moves every reader in its own tick. Never run.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="none 0")
    2: Ui.Label(text="row 2")
    3: Ui.Label(text="some 0")
    4: Ui.Label(text="less 1 more 1")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="none 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="some 2")
    4: Ui.Label(text="less 2 more 3")
